        "Described by Allah as 'The Best of Stories' (Ahsan al-Qasas), the life of Prophet Yusuf (Joseph) is a masterclass in divine providence, chastity, and forgiveness. In childhood, Yusuf witnessed a celestial revelation: ﴿إِذْ قَالَ يُوسُفُ لِأَبِيهِ يَا أَبَتِ إِنِّي رَأَيْتُ أَحَدَ عَشَرَ كَوْكَبًا وَالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ رَأَيْتُهُمْ لِي سَاجِدِينَ﴾ 'When Joseph said to his father, \"O my father, indeed I have seen [in a dream] eleven stars and the sun and the moon; I saw them prostrating to me.\"' (Surah Yusuf 12:4). His father Yaqub recognized the mantle of prophethood and cautioned him against revealing it to his envious elder brothers.",
